Subject: [PATCH] hold a solo grind before an unsafe pull

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

GrindTargetValue returns the first living attacker before it checks possible
candidates, while GrindingStrategy turns an empty target into "attack anything".
Neither decision reads a bot's health, mana or carried water and food. A solo
bot without the needed consumable can therefore start another pull while too
weak to survive it. This patch shares one pure decision between the target gate
and a high-priority rest action. It uses carried inventory counts and never
creates food or drink.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Delete this patch after an equivalent resource hold is merged into the pinned
quadseven/mod-playerbots source and the realm pin advances past that change.

APPLIES TO

quadseven/mod-playerbots @ 40884e9c135c1daf27ffd894a6047502a5701130:
GrindTargetValue, GrindingStrategy and their trigger/action registration.
